Error [E-ERR-SIGIL]: `?` is the retired fallible type separator.
  --> tests/ui/retired_fallible_type_sigil.jet:3:12
    |
  3 | fn f() Int ? E :> Ok(1)
    |            ^
 Why: A fallible type has its own separator so `?` has one meaning: possible absence.
 Fix: Write `T ! E`, such as `Config ! IOError`; write `T !` for the default `Err` type.
